   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# RGB Glitch Text\n\nA short burst where red, green and blue copies of the text jitter apart, then snap back.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A brief digital-glitch hit on a title: a logo sting, a cut, a system-error beat.\n- A short word in bold type where the colour split is the effect.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A sustained glitch is wanted: this one is a burst.\n- A soft or elegant tone: the colour split reads harsh.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"GLITCH\"\n- font_size (number, 12-240): Font size, default 96\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n- glitch_at (number, 0-120): Glitch at, default 20\n- glitch_duration (number, 1-60): Glitch duration, default 8\n- intensity (number, 0-30): Intensity, default 6\n- seed (string): Seed, default \"glitch\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  RGB Glitch Text\n\n  A short burst where red, green and blue copies of the text jitter apart, then snap back.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/rgb-glitch-text/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"rgb-glitch-text\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Text that glitches.\", \"default\": \"GLITCH\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 96, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 240, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"700\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"glitch_at\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Glitch at\", \"description\": \"Frame the glitch starts on.\", \"default\": 20, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"glitch_duration\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Glitch duration\", \"description\": \"How many frames the glitch lasts.\", \"default\": 8, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 60, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"intensity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Intensity\", \"description\": \"Maximum horizontal offset of the colour copies in pixels (at a 96 px font).\", \"default\": 6, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 30, \"step\": 0.5, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"seed\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Seed\", \"description\": \"Same seed draws an identical glitch every time.\", \"default\": \"glitch\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>RGB Glitch Text</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { background: #fafafa; font-family: Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; }\n        .rgt-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .rgt-wrap { position: relative; display: inline-block; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.2; }\n        .rgt-base { position: relative; white-space: pre; color: var(--color, #171717); }\n        .rgt-copy { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; white-space: pre; mix-blend-mode: multiply; opacity: 0; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"rgb-glitch-text\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"rgt-clip\" class=\"rgt-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"rgt-wrap\" class=\"rgt-wrap\" role=\"img\">\n            <span id=\"rgt-base\" class=\"rgt-base\"></span>\n            <span id=\"rgt-r\" class=\"rgt-copy\" style=\"color:#ff0040\"></span>\n            <span id=\"rgt-g\" class=\"rgt-copy\" style=\"color:#00ff80\"></span>\n            <span id=\"rgt-b\" class=\"rgt-copy\" style=\"color:#0080ff\"></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 to 1, rest at 0 velocity (mass, stiffness, damping), at `frame` of 30 fps.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              if (z === 1) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              var q = Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = w0 * (-z + q), r2 = w0 * (-z - q);\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            var TOTAL = 3;\n            var FRAMES = Math.round(TOTAL * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function frameNow() { return Math.round(clock.frame * 1000) / 1000; }\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: FRAMES, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(frameNow()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"rgb-glitch-text\"] = tl;\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            function fit(el, size, frac, hfrac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxW = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              var maxH = Math.max(1, root.clientHeight * (hfrac || 0.9));\n              var k = Math.min(1, maxW / Math.max(1, el.scrollWidth), maxH / Math.max(1, el.scrollHeight));\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(8, size * k); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n\n\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"GLITCH\");\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 96, 12, 240), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var glitchAt = num(vars.glitch_at, 20, 0, 120), glitchDur = num(vars.glitch_duration, 8, 1, 60);\n            var intensity = num(vars.intensity, 6, 0, 30), seed = str(vars.seed, \"glitch\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            var wrap = document.getElementById(\"rgt-wrap\");\n            var els = [\"base\", \"r\", \"g\", \"b\"].map(function (id) { return document.getElementById(\"rgt-\" + id); });\n            els.forEach(function (e) { e.textContent = text; });\n            wrap.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"700\");\n            wrap.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            var fsize = fit(wrap, size, 0.9);\n            onFonts(function () { fsize = fit(wrap, size, 0.9); });\n            // Keep the offsets in proportion to the font size when the text is scaled to fit.\n            function rnd(key) {\n              var h = 1779033703 ^ key.length;\n              for (var i = 0; i < key.length; i++) { h = Math.imul(h ^ key.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353); h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507); h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909); h ^= h >>> 16;\n              return (h >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            start(function (raw) {\n              var frame = raw * speed, key = Math.round(frame);\n              var on = frame >= glitchAt && frame < glitchAt + glitchDur;\n              var sc = fsize / 96;\n              function off(axis, scale) { return (rnd(seed + \"-\" + axis + \"-\" + key) * 2 - 1) * scale * sc; }\n              [[\"r\", 1], [\"g\", 2], [\"b\", 3]].forEach(function (c) {\n                var el = els[c[1]], a = c[0];\n                el.style.opacity = on ? 1 : 0;\n                el.style.transform = on ? \"translate(\" + off(a + \"-x\", intensity) + \"px,\" + off(a + \"-y\", intensity * 0.4) + \"px)\" : \"none\";\n              });\n            });\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
